From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maslow <wangfugen@126.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:34:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Keep fatal diagnostics and scope attribution to every Worker
 entry

V8's location, line and message follow the fatal record as a bounded hex-encoded row of their own. The whole load, each call's JavaScript entry, the native binding's RPC entry and the source JSON check carry a fatal scope; startup, logging and dynamic import entries take the enclosing scope, else the current I/O context's call when it runs the same Worker, else the Worker's load identity, and name nobody on another isolate. The process-wide handler is registered through a role helper that tests drive with a mock registrar; child-process tests reach the isolate's registered handler through V8's own API check. The test build can raise that check while a Worker loads. Includes the test build's api-check event.

